{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011ChPdbLypxndPJon8J5Ruk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"A released job slot, or a raised `max_pods`, now wakes the loops with live demand after a 2-second debounce. `make lint test` passes, and I wrote the report to `.ard/394/worker-engineer.md`.\n\n- **Pool:** the pool now has `Pool.Freed()`, a buffered-1 channel signalled on the first effective `Slot.Release` and when `SetMax` raises the cap. A stale handle whose key was re-granted does not signal. `Pool.DemandLoops(now)` returns the sorted names of loops with live demand and an unheld candidate.\n- **Controller:** a goroutine debounces the freed signals and gives each demand loop one wake. Wakes coalesce with a pending tick and with SIGUSR1, and the pause gate still applies. The wake logs `controller.wake` with `reason=slot_freed`.\n- **Serve:** `internal/servecmd/serve.go` passes the pool lazily, since the pool is built in a startup hook.\n- **Docs:** `docs/proposal.md` now describes the wake in the pool paragraph and the kill-switch paragraph.\n\nI added pool tests and a new `internal/controller/freed_test.go`, all on fake time.\n\n- **Scanner demand:** the issue says scanners keep no demand, but the scanner engine offers with a 10-minute TTL and does keep it. `DemandLoops` therefore skips scanner-class candidates explicitly, so a release never wakes them.\n- **Release timing:** the three job runners release by `defer` after close-out has written its labels, so no path releases early.\n- **Missing re-claim test:** I did not add the separate worker-loop test the plan asked for, where a woken tick must not re-claim the job that just finished. The existing skips for a held key, the `:running` label and a job record are unchanged, and I found no early release path."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":803,"cache_read_input_tokens":42252,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":803},"output_tokens":610,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5ff4ebf2-2666-4434-877a-923cd6f2f050","uuid":"98efc75d-93c9-4ff1-b0eb-1dcd391726c9","timestamp":"2026-11-25T12:17:20.512Z","request_id":"req_011ChPdbLqeWnwHsCfGiRL53"}
